  "body": "**Stacked on #468** (branch `issue/419-thread-dips`, head `d3bb673d`): both change `Script::load`. Only commit `236d40d6` is this issue's work; review that commit. Retarget/refresh after #468 merges.\n\n## What changed (crates/post only)\n- Host prelude, rotary and explanation helpers are evaluated separately from user source (`host.js` / `user.cps`), so syntax and runtime errors report the user's own 1-based line and column, with no prelude offset.\n- Sandbox limits: Boa loop limit 1,000,000 iterations, recursion 64, stack 4,096, kept for every hook call; same on desktop and wasm. A post run is capped at 100,000 output lines counted across hooks; the buffer length is checked in Rust before it is reported or drained, so direct buffer writes cannot slip an oversized program through. Each limit is a named refusal.\n- Host prelude moved to `js_host.rs` (re-exported from `js`, public paths unchanged) to keep `js.rs` under 400 lines (386).\n- New `post::preview`: `BLANK_TEMPLATE` (original, empty hooks, emits nothing), `DEFAULT_VMC_JSON`, and `SAMPLES` - four deterministic sample streams (facing, contour, pocket, drill) built from committed goldens with setup/operation/tool/spindle/clearance records.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/2069-post-sandbox.md`. No new crate dependency.\n\n## Pins\n- `camcraft-post --test script_sandbox` (10): `syntax_errors_report_exact_user_line_and_column`, `runtime_errors_report_exact_user_line_and_column`, `endless_top_level_loop_is_refused`, `endless_hook_loop_is_refused`, `excessive_recursion_is_refused`, `excessive_stack_is_refused`, `output_limit_counts_lines_across_hooks`, `output_limit_covers_every_line_writer`, `direct_output_buffer_writes_are_refused_before_drain`, `direct_output_buffer_writes_are_refused_at_run_boundary`.\n- `camcraft-post --test post_preview` (3): `blank_template_compiles_and_emits_no_lines_or_warnings`, `preview_samples_post_cleanly_and_deterministically`, `preview_samples_carry_setup_operation_tool_spindle_and_cycle_feed`.\nAll 13 pass on `236d40d6` (macOS, m3). The worker checked each pin with a mutation (red without the fix, green with it).\n\n## Known inherited failures (not caused by this PR)\nThe quick gate shows two failures that come from #468's older base:\n- `camcraft-app --test docs_troubleshooting troubleshooting_messages_still_exist_in_the_sources` - panics at `docs_troubleshooting.rs:83` (\"troubleshooting page is readable: NotFound\"). Fixed on main by PR #2053.\n- `camcraft-app --test operations threaded_batch_matches_the_serial_loop_bit_for_bit` - panics at `operations.rs:1433`: APocket3D refuses BN-0600 (the pocket is 20 mm deep but the wider shank starts 15 mm above the tip).\n\nEvidence: both tests were run on #468's head `d3bb673d` with this PR's changes stashed (clean tree, `git status` empty) and both failed with the same messages. This PR changes only `crates/post`; it does not touch the troubleshooting docs or the 3D pocket shank check. Neither failure is fixed here, because the fix belongs on #468's refresh from main (not pushed to #468's branch from this PR).\n\n## Not exercised\n- The UI Post Editor preview wiring (this PR provides the engine-side pieces only).\n- wasm build of the limits (same Boa settings, not built here).\n- Full quick gate beyond the touched post suites and the two app tests above.\n\nFork synced at its current main (upstream merge `09366f64e`).\n\nChangelog: Post engine reports script errors at the user's own line and column, refuses endless loops, deep recursion and oversized output, and provides a blank post template and sample preview streams (#2069).\n\nFixes #2069\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n## Thread controls: before and after\n\nInherited from #468. These Threading Passes tab renders are stored on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\nBefore:\n\n![Threading Passes tab before](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/ebc3d596f234b848ed2392c7cdc180c85afaa918/2115/before.png?raw=true)\n\nAfter:\n\n![Threading Passes tab after](https://github.com/mkinney/Camcraft/blob/ebc3d596f234b848ed2392c7cdc180c85afaa918/2115/after.png?raw=true)\n",
